course: dictionary
lesson: 1047
title: Borrow: take now, give back later
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To borrow is to take something and use it for a while, then give it back. «Borrowing books from the public library is free, and a parent can help you get your own library card.» You take the book home now, and you return it later.
explain: You can borrow money too. It means you get money from a person or a bank and pay it back later. «A girl in Wales called Ella borrowed a library book and lost it; the fine and the cost of the book came out of her savings.» Borrowing means you must give it back, so losing it costs you.
explain: The same word is used in maths. When you take 9 from 23 and there are not enough ones, you borrow 1 ten and make 10 ones. This is also called regrouping. Ask yourself: is something being lent, or is the sum asking you to regroup?
explain: Languages borrow words from each other all the time. «Languages keep changing, borrowing and playing, so the best language skill is curiosity.» When you notice a new word, ask what it means, and enjoy how people talk.
fact: To borrow means to take something now and give it back later.
fact: You can borrow books, toys or money, but you must return them or pay them back.
fact: In subtraction, to borrow means to take 1 ten and make 10 ones.
fact: «Borrow from» shows where something comes from, and «can I borrow» is a polite way to ask.
fact: «Braw» means lovely, and «wee yin» means little one, as Morven says in Edinburgh.
exercise: «Borrowing books from the public library is free.» What does borrowing mean here? | *Taking a book to use and giving it back later | Selling your books | Writing a new book | Buying a book to keep forever
exercise: In 23 minus 9, you need to borrow. What does borrow mean in this sum? | Add 10 more tens | Take away all the tens | *Take 1 ten and make 10 ones | Multiply by 10
exercise: Morven says «braw» about Iona's hair clips. Which word means the same? | *lovely | empty | grey | loud
test: Which sentence shows borrowing money? | I gave money away as a gift | I found money in the street and kept it | I saved money in a jar | *I got money from the bank and will pay it back later
test: Which word means to take something now and give it back later? | *borrow | library card | fine | savings
exam: «Jayden borrows his sister's bike for the day.» What does borrows mean here? | *Takes it to use and will give it back | Buys it for keeps | Sells it | Breaks it
